- So''roq: Am / Is / Are + Subject + Verb-ing?
Vaqt ko''rsatkichlari: now (hozir), at the moment (ayni paytda), currently, right now, Look!, Listen!
MUHIM: State verbs (holat fe''llari) his-tuyg''u, aqliy faoliyat va egalikni bildirib, odatda Continuous zamonlarda ISHLATILMAYDI: know, understand, believe, love, like, hate, want, need, remember, belong, see, hear. Masalan: ''I understand you'' (I am understanding emas).', '[{"title": "Present Continuous qo''llanishi", "problem": "''Listen! Somebody (sing) in the garden'' gapini to''ldiring.", "step_by_step": "''Listen!'' ayni daqiqadagi harakatga e''tiborni qaratmoqda. Somebody (3-shaxs birlik) -> is singing.", "answer": "Listen! Somebody is singing in the garden"}, {"title": "State verbs qoidasi", "problem": "''I (not / believe) this strange story'' gapini to''g''ri zamonda yozing.", "step_by_step": "''Believe'' fe''li aqliy ishonchni bildiruvchi holat fe''li bo''lib, Continuous bo''lmaydi. Present Simple ishlatiladi: ''I don''t believe''.", "answer": "I don''t believe this strange story"}]'::jsonb, 'Taqqoslang: ''Look! It (rain)'' vs ''It usually (rain) in autumn.''', '''Look! It is raining'' (ayni paytda) va ''It usually rains in autumn'' (odatdagi holat).', '[{"question": "Qaysi fe''l odatda Present Continuous zamonida ishlatilmaydi?", "options": ["run", "know", "eat", "write"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "''Know'' (bilmoq) aqliy holat fe''li bo''lib, davomli zamon qo''shimchasini olmaydi."}, {"question": "''They ... dinner right now'' gapiga qaysi shakl to''g''ri keladi?", "options": ["have", "are having", "is having", "has"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "''Right now'' davomli zamon talab qiladi, ''They'' bilan ''are having'' qo''llanadi."}, {"question": "Present Continuous zamonining so''roq shakli qanday yasaladi?", "options": ["Do/Does + ega + V1", "Am/Is/Are + ega + V-ing", "Did + ega + V1", "Have + ega + V3"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "To be (am/is/are) yordamchi fe''li egadan oldinga o''tadi."}]'::jsonb, '["english", "grammar", "present continuous", "stative verbs", "A2", "6-sinf"]'::jsonb, 30) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
1) Regular verbs (to''g''ri fe''llar): fe''lga -ed qo''shiladi (work -> worked, play -> played, study -> studied);
2) Irregular verbs (noto''g''ri fe''llar): maxsus o''zgaradi (go -> went, see -> saw, buy -> bought, have -> had, write -> wrote).
Formulalar:
- Darak: Subject + V2 (I visited London last year; She bought a new car);
- Inkor: Subject + did not (didn''t) + V1 (fe''l 1-shaklga qaytadi: She didn''t buy);
- So''roq: Did + Subject + V1? (Did you see that movie?).
Vaqt ko''rsatkichlari: yesterday (kecha), last week/month/year (o''tgan hafta/yil), in 2015, two days ago (ikki kun oldin).', '[{"title": "Inkor va so''roqqa aylantirish", "problem": "''He wrote a letter yesterday'' gapini inkor va maxsus so''roq shakliga o''tkazing.", "step_by_step": "1) Inkor: He didn''t write a letter yesterday (wrote -> write bo''ladi).\n2) So''roq: What did he write yesterday?", "answer": "He didn''t write... / What did he write yesterday?"}, {"title": "To be fe''lining o''tgan zamoni", "problem": "''They (be) at the museum on Sunday'' gapini to''ldiring.", "step_by_step": "''To be'' ning o''tgan zamoni I/he/she/it uchun WAS, we/you/they uchun WERE bo''ladi. ''They were at the museum...''", "answer": "They were at the museum on Sunday"}]'::jsonb, 'Noto''g''ri fe''llarning V2 shaklini yozing: eat, make, take, leave, fly.', 'ate, made, took, left, flew.', '[{"question": "''Go'' fe''lining Past Simple (V2) shakli qaysi?", "options": ["goed", "gone", "went", "goes"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "''Go'' noto''g''ri fe''l bo''lib, o''tgan zamoni ''went'' dir."}, {"question": "Past Simple inkorda ''didn''t'' dan keyin fe''l qaysi shaklda keladi?", "options": ["V2 (o''tgan zamon)", "V1 (boshlang''ich shakl)", "V-ing", "V3"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "''Did'' o''tgan zamon yukini o''ziga olgani sababli asosiy fe''l V1 (infinitive) ga qaytadi."}, {"question": "I, He, She, It uchun ''to be'' ning o''tgan zamoni qaysi?", "options": ["were", "was", "been", "are"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Birlik shaxslar uchun ''was'', ko''plik uchun ''were'' ishlatiladi."}]'::jsonb, '["english", "past simple", "irregular verbs", "grammar", "A2", "7-sinf"]'::jsonb, 30) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
Formulalar:
- Darak: Subject + have / has + V3 (Past Participle) (I have seen, He has finished);
- Inkor: Subject + haven''t / hasn''t + V3;
- So''roq: Have / Has + Subject + V3?
Signal so''zlar:
- just (hozirgina), already (allaqachon) — darak gapda;
- yet (hali) — faqat inkor va so''roq gap oxirida;
- ever (hech/umringda) — so''roqda; never (hech qachon) — inkorda;
- for (davomida: for 5 years) va since (berli, boshlanish vaqti: since 2018).', '[{"title": "Hayotiy tajriba haqida so''rash", "problem": "''Siz hech qachon samolyotda uchganmisiz?'' jumlasini ingliz tiliga tarjima qiling.", "step_by_step": "Hayotiy tajriba uchun ''Have you ever + V3'' qolipi ishlatiladi. Fly fe''lining V3 shakli ''flown''.\nNatija: ''Have you ever flown by plane?''", "answer": "Have you ever flown by plane?"}, {"title": "Since va for farqi", "problem": "''I have lived in Tashkent (for / since) 10 years'' gapida qaysi ko''rsatkich to''g''ri?", "step_by_step": "''10 years'' bu vaqt davomiyligi (muddat), shuning uchun ''for'' ishlatiladi. Agar boshlang''ich yil (masalan: 2014) bo''lsa ''since'' bo''lardi.", "answer": "for 10 years"}]'::jsonb, '''I (already / finish) my homework, but my brother (not / do) his yet'' gapini to''ldiring.', '''I have already finished my homework, but my brother hasn''t done his yet.''', '[{"question": "''Yet'' so''zi qanday gaplarda va gapning qaysi qismida ishlatiladi?", "options": ["Faqat darak gap o''rtasida", "Inkor va so''roq gap oxirida", "Faqat o''tgan zamonda", "Gap boshida"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "''Yet'' faqat inkor va so''roq gaplarning eng oxirida keladi: ''I haven''t eaten yet''."}, {"question": "Present Perfect da ''see'' fe''lining 3-shakli (Past Participle) qaysi?", "options": ["saw", "seen", "seeing", "sees"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "see (V1) - saw (V2) - seen (V3)."}, {"question": "Past Simple va Present Perfect ning asosiy farqi nima?", "options": ["Hech qanday farqi yo''q", "Past Simple da vaqt aniq ko''rsatiladi (yesterday), Present Perfect da natija muhim", "Past Simple faqat savollarda ishlatiladi", "Present Perfect faqat kelasi zamonda"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Past Simple da o''tmishdagi aniq vaqt aytiladi, Present Perfect da esa harakatning hozirgi kundagi natijasi/tajribasi muhim."}]'::jsonb, '["english", "present perfect", "grammar", "since", "for", "B1", "8-sinf"]'::jsonb, 35) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
Umumiy formula: Object + TO BE (mos zamonda) + V3 (Past Participle) (+ by Subject).
Zamonlar bo''yicha:
- Present Simple Passive: am / is / are + V3 (English is spoken all over the world);
- Past Simple Passive: was / were + V3 (The bridge was built in 1995);
- Future Simple Passive: will be + V3 (The work will be finished tomorrow);
- Present Perfect Passive: have / has been + V3 (The car has been repaired).
Modal fe''llar: can/could (qobiliyat), must (qat''iy qonuniy majburiyat), have to (zaruriyat), should (maslahat: ''You should see a doctor''), may/might (ehtimollik/ruxsat). Modal fe''llardan keyin ''to'' siz sof fe''l (bare infinitive) keladi.', '[{"title": "Active dan Passive ga o''tkazish", "problem": "''Alexander Bell invented the telephone in 1876'' gapini Passive Voice ga aylantiring.", "step_by_step": "1) Obyekt: ''The telephone'' gap boshiga chiqadi;\n2) Zamon: Past Simple -> was invented;\n3) Bajaruvchi: by Alexander Bell;\nNatija: ''The telephone was invented by Alexander Bell in 1876''.", "answer": "The telephone was invented by Alexander Bell in 1876"}, {"title": "Must vs Should farqi", "problem": "''You (must / should) stop when the traffic light is red'' — qaysi modal fe''l to''g''ri?", "step_by_step": "Qizil chiroqda to''xtash bu tavsiya emas, qat''iy yo''l harakati qoidasi (majburiyat), shuning uchun ''must'' ishlatiladi.", "answer": "must"}]'::jsonb, 'Passive Voice ga aylantiring: ''They clean the rooms every day.''', '''The rooms are cleaned every day.''', '[{"question": "Passive Voice hosil qilishning umumiy formulasi qaysi?", "options": ["have + V3", "to be + V3 (Past Participle)", "to be + V-ing", "will + V1"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Majhul nisbat har doim ''to be'' ning tegishli zamon shakli va fe''lning 3-shakli (V3) bilan yasaladi."}, {"question": "Maslahat berishda qaysi modal fe''l ishlatiladi?", "options": ["must", "can", "should", "may"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "''Should'' do''stona maslahat va tavsiya berish uchun qo''llanadi (''You should sleep more'')."}, {"question": "''The Mona Lisa ... painted by Leonardo da Vinci'' — nuqtalar o''rniga nima qo''yiladi?", "options": ["is", "was", "were", "has"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Rasm o''tmishda bitta jism sifatida yaratilgani uchun ''was painted'' bo''ladi."}]'::jsonb, '["english", "passive voice", "modal verbs", "grammar", "B1", "9-sinf"]'::jsonb, 35) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
1) Zero Conditional (100% haqiqat, tabiiy qonunlar):
   If + Present Simple, Present Simple. (''If you heat ice, it melts'' — Muzni qizdirsangiz, u eriydi).
2) First Conditional (Kelajakdagi real ehtimoliy shart):
   If + Present Simple, will + V1. (''If it rains tomorrow, we will stay at home'' — Agar ertaga yomg''ir yog''sa, biz uyda qolamiz).
3) Second Conditional (Hozirgi paytdagi xayoliy, noreal orzu-istak):
   If + Past Simple, would + V1. (Barcha shaxslar uchun ''were'' afzal: ''If I were you, I would study harder'' — Sizning o''rningizda bo''lganimda ko''proq o''qirdim; ''If I won a million dollars, I would travel'').
4) Third Conditional (O''tmishda bajarilmagan noreal shart va afsus):
   If + Past Perfect (had + V3), would have + V3. (''If I had studied harder, I would have passed the exam'' — Ko''proq o''qiganimda edi, imtihondan o''tgan bo''lardim).', '[{"title": "First Conditional vs Second Conditional", "problem": "''If I have free time tonight, I (watch) a movie'' va ''If I had a spaceship, I (fly) to Mars'' gaplarini oching.", "step_by_step": "1) Bugun oqshomda vaqt bo''lishi real ehtimol -> First Conditional: will watch;\n2) Kosmik kema bo''lishi hozir noreal orzu -> Second Conditional: would fly.", "answer": "will watch / would fly"}, {"title": "Third Conditional (o''tmishdagi afsus)", "problem": "''We missed the train because we woke up late'' vaziyatiga Third Conditional tuzing.", "step_by_step": "Formula: If + had + V3, would have + V3.\nNatija: ''If we hadn''t woken up late, we wouldn''t have missed the train''.", "answer": "If we hadn''t woken up late, we wouldn''t have missed the train"}]'::jsonb, 'Qavslarni oching: ''If she (know) the truth back then, she (not / make) that mistake.''', '''If she had known the truth back then, she wouldn''t have made that mistake'' (Third Conditional).', '[{"question": "First Conditional da ''If'' li qismda qaysi zamon ishlatiladi?", "options": ["Future Simple (will)", "Present Simple", "Past Simple", "Present Perfect"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Qoidaga ko''ra ''If'' li shart ergash qismida ''will'' ishlatilmaydi, Present Simple qo''llanadi."}, {"question": "Hozirgi zamondagi noreal orzu-istakni ifodalovchi shart turi qaysi?", "options": ["Zero Conditional", "First Conditional", "Second Conditional", "Third Conditional"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "Second Conditional (If + Past Simple, would + V1) xayoliy noreal vaziyatlar uchun qo''llanadi."}, {"question": "''If I were a bird, I would fly'' gapida nima uchun ''was'' o''rniga ''were'' ishlatiladi?", "options": ["Chunki bu qoida xatosi", "Subjunctive mood (istak mayli) da barcha shaxslar uchun ''were'' qo''llanishi adabiy me''yordir", "Chunki ''I'' ko''plik olmoshi", "Faqat qushlar bilan shunday"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Second Conditional da rasmiy va adabiy me''yorda ''I'' va ''He/She'' bilan ham ''were'' qo''llanadi."}]'::jsonb, '["english", "conditionals", "if clauses", "grammar", "B2", "10-sinf"]'::jsonb, 35) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
Klassik 4 qismli struktura:
1. Introduction (2 gap): Paraphrase the prompt (savolni o''z so''zlari bilan qayta yozish) + Thesis Statement (shaxsiy pozitsiya va inshoning qisqacha maqsadi);
2. Body Paragraph 1 (Topic sentence + Explanation + Concrete Example);
3. Body Paragraph 2 (Topic sentence + Explanation + Concrete Example);
4. Conclusion (Summary of main points + Final recommendation). Bog''lovchi vositalar (Cohesive devices): Furthermore, However, Consequently, For instance, In contrast, On the other hand.', '[{"title": "Savolni parafraz qilish (Paraphrasing)", "problem": "Mavzu: ''Some people think that universities should provide graduates with knowledge and skills for their future jobs.'' Ushbu gapni kirish qismida parafraz qiling.", "step_by_step": "Sinonimlar va struktura o''zgarishi: Some people believe -> It is often argued; provide with skills -> equip students with practical competencies; future jobs -> prospective careers.\nParafraz: ''It is widely argued that higher education institutions ought to equip learners with the practical competencies necessary for their prospective careers.''", "answer": "It is widely argued that higher education institutions ought to equip learners with practical competencies..."}, {"title": "Thesis Statement tuzish", "problem": "''To what extent do you agree or disagree?'' savoliga qat''iy fikrli (strong thesis) gap yozing.", "step_by_step": "''This essay completely agrees with this perspective, as vocational preparedness enhances graduate employability and directly stimulates economic growth.''", "answer": "This essay completely agrees with this perspective, as..."}]'::jsonb, 'Body paragraf uchun ''Topic Sentence'' ning vazifasi nima va u qanday yoziladi?', 'Topic Sentence paragrafning birinchi gapi bo''lib, butun paragrafda qanday asosiy g''oya muhokama qilinishini aniq va lo''nda e''lon qiladi.', '[{"question": "IELTS Writing Task 2 da insho hajmi kamida nechta so''zdan iborat bo''lishi shart?", "options": ["150 ta", "200 ta", "250 ta", "300 ta"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "Task 2 uchun minimal hajm 250 ta so''z; kam bo''lsa Task Response dan ball tushiriladi."}, {"question": "Kirish (Introduction) paragrafining eng muhim gapi nima deyiladi?", "options": ["Topic sentence", "Thesis statement", "Example", "Conclusion"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Thesis statement muallifning mavzuga nisbatan bosh pozitsiyasini bildiruvchi asosiy gapdir."}, {"question": "Insho oxiridagi Conclusion (xulosa) qismida yangi g''oyalar yoki dalillar kiritilishi to''g''rimi?", "options": ["Ha, albatta", "Yo''q, xulosada faqat oldingi fikrlar umumlashtiriladi", "Ixtiyoriy", "Faqat muammoli mavzuda"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Xulosada hech qachon yangi g''oya berilmaydi, faqat tana paragraflaridagi fikrlar yakunlanadi."}]'::jsonb, '["english", "ielts", "writing task 2", "academic essay", "B2-C1", "11-sinf"]'::jsonb, 35) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
- ''make'' bilan: make a decision, make progress, make an effort, make a mistake;
- ''do'' bilan: do research, do homework, do business, do someone a favor;
- Sifat + Ot: heavy rain (kuchli yomg''ir, strong rain emas), rapid growth, significant impact, vital role.
Phrasal Verbs (Iborali fe''llar) — fe''l va predlog/ravishdan iborat bo''lib, yangi ko''chma ma''no hosil qiladi: carry out (amalga oshirmoq / to conduct: carry out research), bring about (sabab bo''lmoq / to cause), look forward to (intiqlik bilan kutmoq), turn down (rad etmoq / to reject), give up (tashlamoq / to quit), run out of (tugab qolmoq).', '[{"title": "Do va Make kollokatsiyalari", "problem": "''Scientists are (making / doing) research on renewable energy'' — qaysi fe''l to''g''ri?", "step_by_step": "''Research'' so''zi bilan har doim ''do'' ishlatiladi (do research, conduct research). ''Make research'' grammatik xato hisoblanadi.", "answer": "doing research"}, {"title": "Phrasal verb ma''nosini ochish", "problem": "''The government decided to call off the strike'' gapidagi ''call off'' nimani anglatadi?", "step_by_step": "''Call off'' iborali fe''li bekor qilmoq (to cancel) ma''nosini bildiradi.", "answer": "Bekor qilmoq (to cancel)"}]'::jsonb, 'Bo''sh o''rinni to''ldiring: ''Education plays a ... role in personal development.'' (vital / strong / heavy)', '''vital role'' (juda muhim rol o''ynamoq; play a vital/pivotal role).', '[{"question": "''Xatoga yo''l qo''ymoq'' birikmasi ingliz tilida qanday bo''ladi?", "options": ["do a mistake", "make a mistake", "create a mistake", "take a mistake"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Qat''iy kollokatsiya qoidasiga ko''ra ''make a mistake'' ishlatiladi."}, {"question": "''Carry out'' iborali fe''lining ma''nosi nima?", "options": ["Yuk ko''tarmoq", "Amalga oshirmoq, o''tkazmoq (to conduct)", "Tashqariga chiqmoq", "Rad etmoq"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "''Carry out an experiment/research'' — tadqiqot yoki tajriba o''tkazmoq degan ma''noni beradi."}, {"question": "''Give up'' iborasi nimani anglatadi?", "options": ["Sovg''a qilmoq", "Tashlab yubormoq, taslim bo''lmoq", "Davom ettirmoq", "Boshlamoq"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "''Give up'' biror odatni tashlash yoki kurashdan voz kechishni bildiradi."}]'::jsonb, '["english", "vocabulary", "collocations", "phrasal verbs", "C1", "11-sinf"]'::jsonb, 30) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
1) Мужской род (он, мой): qattiq undoshga yoki -й ga tugaydi (стол, дом, музей, учитель);
2) Женский род (она, моя): -а, -я yoki yumshatish belgili asoslarga tugaydi (книга, земля, песня, ночь);
3) Средний род (оно, моё): -о, -е, -мя ga tugaydi (окно, поле, море, время, имя).
Turlanish (склонение):
- 1-склонение: -а, -я bilan tugaydigan ayol va erkak jinsidagi otlar (мама, папа, книга, земля);
- 2-склонение: nol qo''shimchali erkak jinsi va -о, -е li o''rta jins otlari (стол, конь, окно, море);
- 3-склонение: -ь (yumshatish belgisi) bilan tugaydigan ayol jinsidagi otlar (ночь, мышь, тетрадь, радость).', '[{"title": "Otning rodini aniqlash", "problem": "''Время'', ''словарь'' va ''тетрадь'' so''zlarining jinsini (род) aniqlang.", "step_by_step": "1) Время — -мя bilan tugagan, demak средний род (оно моё);\n2) Словарь — erkak jinsidagi ot (он мой, родительный: словаря — 2-склонение);\n3) Тетрадь — ayol jinsidagi ot (она моя, родительный: тетради — 3-склонение).", "answer": "Время - ср.р., Словарь - м.р., Тетрадь - ж.р."}, {"title": "Mening (мой/моя/моё) olmoshini moslashtirish", "problem": "''(Мой) семья'', ''(мой) брат'' va ''(мой) пальто'' birikmalarini to''g''rilang.", "step_by_step": "Семья (ж.р.) -> моя семья; Брат (м.р.) -> мой брат; Пальто (ср.р., o''zgarmas) -> моё пальто.", "answer": "Моя семья, мой брат, моё пальто"}]'::jsonb, 'So''zlarni turlanishlar (склонение) bo''yicha ajrating: школа, город, дочь, дядя, озеро.', '1-склонение: школа, дядя; 2-склонение: город, озеро; 3-склонение: дочь.', '[{"question": "-о va -е bilan tugaydigan otlar odatda qaysi jinsga kiradi?", "options": ["Мужской род", "Женский род", "Средний род", "Umumiy rod"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "-о va -е bilan tugovchi otlar sredniy rod hisoblanadi (masalan: окно, море)."}, {"question": "3-склонение ga qaysi otlar kiradi?", "options": ["-а, -я li otlar", "Undoshga tugaydigan erkak jinsi", "-ь bilan tugaydigan ayol jinsi otlari", "Barcha o''rta jins"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "3-skloneniyaga faqat yumshatish belgisi (-ь) bilan tugovchi ayol jinsidagi otlar kiradi (ночь, мать)."}, {"question": "''Кофе'' so''zi rus adabiy tilida qaysi jinsda qo''llanadi?", "options": ["Средний род", "Мужской род", "Женский род", "Ko''plikda"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Qat''iy adabiy normaga ko''ra ''чёрный кофе'' erkak jinsidadir (он мой)."}]'::jsonb, '["rus tili", "род", "склонение", "грамматика", "5-sinf"]'::jsonb, 25) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
1) Именительный (Bosh kelishik: Кто? Что?) — gapda doimo ega bo''ladi (Студент читает);
2) Родительный (Kimning? Nimaning? Kim/nima yo''q? Кого? Чего?) — predloglar: без, для, до, из, от, у, около (нет книги, стакан воды);
3) Дательный (Jo''nalish: Кому? Чему?) — predloglar: к, по (подарить другу, подойти к окну);
4) Винительный (Tushum: Кого? Что?) — predloglar: в, на, через (читать книгу, вижу друга);
5) Творительный (Birgalik/qurol: Кем? Чем?) — predloglar: с, под, над, за, перед (писать ручкой, гулять с другом);
6) Предложный (O''rin-payt: О ком? О чём? Где?) — doimo predlog bilan keladi: о/об, в, на (думать о родине, жить в Ташкенте).', '[{"title": "Padejni to''g''ri qo''llash", "problem": "''Я живу в (Ташкент) и учусь в (школа)'' gapidagi qavslarni oching.", "step_by_step": "''Где?'' savoliga javob beruvchi o''rin ma''nosi Предложный падеж talab qiladi (qo''shimcha -е):\nТашкент -> в Ташкенте; школа -> в школе.", "answer": "Я живу в Ташкенте и учусь в школе"}, {"title": "Родительный падеж inkorda", "problem": "''У меня есть время'' gapini inkor shaklga o''giring.", "step_by_step": "Inkor qilinganda ''нет'' so''zidan keyin Родительный падеж ishlatiladi: время -> времени.\nNatija: ''У меня нет времени''.", "answer": "У меня нет времени"}]'::jsonb, '''Друг'' so''zini Творительный падежда ''с'' predlogi bilan ishlating.', 'с другом (гулять с другом).', '[{"question": "Faqat predloglar bilan ishlatiladigan yagona padej qaysi?", "options": ["Родительный", "Дательный", "Творительный", "Предложный"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "Предложный падеж hech qachon predlogsiz (о, в, на, при) qo''llanmaydi."}, {"question": "''Кому? Чему?'' qaysi padejning so''roqlari?", "options": ["Дательный", "Винительный", "Родительный", "Творительный"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Дательный падеж jo''nalish va berish harakatini bildiradi (дать кому?)."}, {"question": "Jonli otlarda Винительный падеж shakli qaysi padej bilan bir xil bo''ladi?", "options": ["Именительный", "Родительный", "Дательный", "Предложный"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Jonli erkak jinsidagi otlarda Винительный shakli Родительный bilan bir xil (вижу студента = нет студента)."}]'::jsonb, '["rus tili", "падежи", "грамматика", "предлоги", "7-sinf"]'::jsonb, 35) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
1) Несовершенный вид (НСВ) — savoli: Что делать? Harakatning davomiyligini, jarayonini yoki doimiy takrorlanishini bildiradi (читать, писать, делать). Bu fe''llar 3 ta zamonga ega: o''tgan (читал), hozirgi (читаю) va murakkab kelasi (буду читать);
2) Совершенный вид (СВ) — savoli: Что сделать? Harakatning tugallanganligini, bir martalikligini va natijaga erishilganini bildiradi (прочитать, написать, сделать). Bu fe''llarning hozirgi zamoni YO''Q, faqat o''tgan (прочитал) va oddiy kelasi zamoni (прочитаю) bo''ladi.
Vid juftliklari ko''pincha prefikslar (yondash qo''shimchalar) yordamida yasaladi: писать -> написать, учить -> выучить, делать -> сделать.', '[{"title": "Vidni to''g''ri tanlash", "problem": "''Я вчера два часа (читал / прочитал) книгу'' — qaysi fe''l to''g''ri?", "step_by_step": "''Два часа'' (ikki soat davomida) harakatning davomiy jarayon ekanligini ko''rsatmoqda, shuning uchun НСВ kerak: ''читал''.", "answer": "читал"}, {"title": "Natijani ifodalash", "problem": "''Men uy vazifamni bajarib bo''ldim'' jumlasini tarjima qiling.", "step_by_step": "Harakat yakunlangan va natija bor. ''Сделать'' (СВ) fe''li ishlatiladi: ''Я сделал домашнее задание''.", "answer": "Я сделал домашнее задание"}]'::jsonb, 'Fe''llarni vid juftliklariga ajrating: решать — ..., открывать — ..., повторять — ...', 'решать — решить, открывать — открыть, повторять — повторить.', '[{"question": "Совершенный вид fe''llarining qaysi zamon shakli mavjud emas?", "options": ["O''tgan zamon", "Hozirgi zamon", "Kelasi zamon", "Hech qaysi"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Совершенный вид tugallanganlikni bildirgani uchun unda hozirgi zamon shakli umuman bo''lmaydi."}, {"question": "Harakatning jarayonini va takrorlanishini qaysi vid bildiradi?", "options": ["Совершенный вид", "Несовершенный вид", "Har ikkalasi", "Hech biri"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Несовершенный вид (что делать?) jarayon va takrorlanishni ifodalaydi."}, {"question": "''Буду писать'' qaysi zamon va qaysi vid shakli?", "options": ["Совершенный вид kelasi zamon", "Несовершенный вид murakkab kelasi zamon", "O''tgan zamon", "Hozirgi zamon"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "''Буду + infinitiv'' faqat несовершенный вид ning murakkab kelasi zamonida ishlatiladi."}]'::jsonb, '["rus tili", "вид глагола", "совершенный", "несовершенный", "8-sinf"]'::jsonb, 30) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
1) Piyoda harakatlanish: идти (bir tomonga, ayni daqiqada: ''Я иду в школу'') — ходить (har doim, har xil tomonga yoki borib-kelish: ''Я каждый день хожу в школу'');
2) Transportda harakatlanish: ехать (bir tomonga ayni paytda: ''Мы едем в Самарканд'') — ездить (muntazam: ''Мы часто ездим в горы'');
Prefikslar bilan ma''no o''zgarishi:
- по- (harakat boshlanishi: пойти, поехать);
- при- (yetib kelish: прийти, приехать);
- у- (ketish, jo''nash: уйти, уехать);
- в- / во- (ichkariga kirish: войти в комнату);
- вы- (tashqariga chiqish: выйти из класса);
- пере- (kesib o''tish: перейти улицу).', '[{"title": "Идти va ходить farqi", "problem": "''Смотри, куда он ...?'' va ''Он каждую субботу ... в бассейн'' gaplarini to''ldiring.", "step_by_step": "1) ''Смотри, куда он идёт?'' (ayni paytdagi aniq bir yo''nalish);\n2) ''Он каждую субботу ходит в бассейн'' (muntazam takrorlanuvchi harakat).", "answer": "идёт / ходит"}, {"title": "Prefiksli harakat fe''li", "problem": "''Poyezd soat 8 da Toshkentga yetib keldi'' jumlasini rus tiliga o''giring.", "step_by_step": "Transportda yetib kelish uchun ''при-'' prefiksi va ''ехать'' fe''li ishlatiladi: ''Поезд прибыл (приехал) в Ташкент в 8 часов''.", "answer": "Поезд приехал в Ташкент в 8 часов"}]'::jsonb, 'Prefikslar ma''nosini moslang: войти, выйти, перейти (chiqmoq, kirmoq, kesib o''tmoq).', 'войти — kirmoq; выйти — chiqmoq; перейти — kesib o''tmoq.', '[{"question": "Piyoda bir yo''nalishda ayni paytda borayotganda qaysi fe''l ishlatiladi?", "options": ["ходить", "идти", "ехать", "ездить"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "''Идти'' ayni daqiqadagi bir yo''nalishli piyoda harakatni bildiradi."}, {"question": "Ko''chani kesib o''tishda qaysi prefiksli fe''l qo''llanadi?", "options": ["войти", "уйти", "перейти", "прийти"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "''Пере-'' prefiksi bir tarafdan ikkinchi tarafga kesib o''tishni bildiradi (перейти дорогу)."}, {"question": "Transport vositasida muntazam qatnashni qaysi fe''l ifodalaydi?", "options": ["ехать", "ездить", "идти", "ходить"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "''Ездить'' transportda doimiy yoki ikki tomonga qatnashni bildiradi."}]'::jsonb, '["rus tili", "глаголы движения", "идти", "ехать", "префиксы", "9-sinf"]'::jsonb, 35) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
1) Maskulin (erkak jinsi) — der Tisch, der Mann (noaniq: ein);
2) Feminin (ayol jinsi) — die Frau, die Lampe (noaniq: eine);
3) Neytral (o''rta jins) — das Buch, das Kind (noaniq: ein);
4) Ko''plik (Plural) — die Bücher, die Tische (noaniq artikl yo''q).
4 ta kelishik (Kasus):
- Nominativ (Bosh kelishik: Wer? Was?) — der, die, das, die;
- Akkusativ (Tushum: Wen? Was?) — faqat erkak jinsi o''zgaradi: den (einen), die (eine), das (ein), die;
- Dativ (Jo''nalish: Wem? Wo?): dem (einem), der (einer), dem (einem), den...n;
- Genitiv (Qaratqich: Wessen?): des...s, der, des...s, der.', '[{"title": "Akkusativ kelishigida artikl o''zgarishi", "problem": "''Ich habe ... (der Hund)'' gapida qaysi artikl bo''ladi?", "step_by_step": "Haben fe''li doimo Akkusativ (tushum) talab qiladi. Der Hund erkak jinsida ''den Hund'' yoki noaniq ''einen Hund'' ga aylanadi.\nNatija: ''Ich habe einen Hund''.", "answer": "einen Hund (den Hund)"}, {"title": "Dativ kelishigida o''rin bildirish", "problem": "''Das Buch liegt auf ... (der Tisch)'' — kitob stol ustida yotibdi (qayerda? — Dativ).", "step_by_step": "''Wo?'' (qayerda?) savoliga javob berganda ''auf'' predlogi Dativ talab qiladi. Der Tisch -> dem Tisch.\nNatija: ''Das Buch liegt auf dem Tisch''.", "answer": "auf dem Tisch"}]'::jsonb, 'Nemis tilida ''die Schule'' (maktab) so''zini 4 ta kelishikda aniq artikl bilan yozing.', 'Nom: die Schule, Akk: die Schule, Dat: der Schule, Gen: der Schule.', '[{"question": "Akkusativ kelishigida qaysi jinsdagi aniq artikl ''den'' ga o''zgaradi?", "options": ["Feminin (die)", "Maskulin (der)", "Neutral (das)", "Plural (die)"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Akkusativda faqat erkak jinsi ''der'' -> ''den'' (yoki ein -> einen) ga o''zgaradi."}, {"question": "Nemis tilida otlar qanday harf bilan yoziladi?", "options": ["Faqat gap boshida bosh harf bilan", "Doimo bosh (katta) harf bilan", "Kichik harf bilan", "Ixtiyoriy"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Nemis tili orfografiyasiga ko''ra barcha otlar gapning qayerida kelishidan qat''i nazar bosh harf bilan yoziladi."}, {"question": "''Wem?'' (kimgacha?) qaysi nemischa kelishikning so''rog''i?", "options": ["Nominativ", "Akkusativ", "Dativ", "Genitiv"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "''Wem?'' Dativ (uchinchi kelishik) so''rog''idir."}]'::jsonb, '["nemis tili", "artikl", "kasus", "akkusativ", "dativ", "A1", "6-sinf"]'::jsonb, 25) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
- ''Sein'' yordamchi fe''li bilan: joy o''zgarishi (harakat fe''llari: gehen, fahren, fliegen, kommen) va holat o''zgarishi (aufstehen, sterben) hamda sein, bleiben fe''llari ishlatiladi: ''Ich bin nach Berlin gefahren'';
- Qolgan barcha holatlarda ''haben'' ishlatiladi: ''Ich habe ein Buch gelesen''.
Partizip II yasalishi: ge- + o''zak + -(e)t (to''g''ri fe''llarda: gemacht, gespielt); ge- + o''zak + -en (noto''g''ri fe''llarda: gelesen, geschrieben).
Modal fe''llar: können (qila olmoq), müssen (majbur bo''lmoq), wollen (xohlamoq), dürfen (ruxsat bo''lmoq), sollen (kerak bo''lmoq). Gapda modal fe''l 2-o''rinda keladi, asosiy fe''l esa infintiv shaklda gap oxiriga suriladi: ''Ich kann Deutsch sprechen''.', '[{"title": "Perfektda jumla tuzish", "problem": "''Er (machen) seine Hausaufgaben gestern'' gapini Perfektda tuzing.", "step_by_step": "1) Machen harakat yoki holat o''zgarishi emas, demak yordamchi fe''l: haben -> er hat;\n2) Partizip II: gemacht;\n3) Gap oxiriga suriladi: ''Er hat gestern seine Hausaufgaben gemacht''.", "answer": "Er hat gestern seine Hausaufgaben gemacht"}, {"title": "Harakat fe''lida ''sein''", "problem": "''Wir (fahren) nach Deutschland'' gapini Perfektda tuzing.", "step_by_step": "Fahren transportda joy o''zgarishi, shuning uchun ''sein'' olinadi: wir sind. Partizip II: gefahren.\nNatija: ''Wir sind nach Deutschland gefahren''.", "answer": "Wir sind nach Deutschland gefahren"}]'::jsonb, 'Modal fe''l bilan gap tuzing: ''Ich / wollen / ein neues Auto / kaufen''.', '''Ich will ein neues Auto kaufen'' (modal fe''l will 2-o''rinda, kaufen gap oxirida).', '[{"question": "Perfekt zamonida asosiy ma''noli fe''l (Partizip II) gapning qayerida joylashadi?", "options": ["Yordamchi fe''lning yonida", "Gap boshida", "Gapning eng oxirida", "Ixtiyoriy joyda"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "Nemis tilidagi ramka (Satzklammer) qoidasiga ko''ra Partizip II gapning eng oxirida turadi."}, {"question": "''Gehen'' (bormoq) fe''li Perfektda qaysi yordamchi fe''l bilan qo''llanadi?", "options": ["haben", "sein", "werden", "können"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Piyoda joy o''zgarishi bo''lgani sababli ''sein'' bilan keladi: ''Ich bin gegangen''."}, {"question": "''Können'' modal fe''lining ''ich'' (men) shaxsi uchun hozirgi zamon shakli qaysi?", "options": ["kann", "könne", "konnte", "kannst"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Modal fe''llarda 1- va 3-shaxs birlik bir xil va qo''shimchasiz bo''ladi: ich kann, er kann."}]'::jsonb, '["nemis tili", "perfekt", "modalverben", "haben sein", "A2", "8-sinf"]'::jsonb, 30) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
1) I guruh (-er bilan tugovchi to''g''ri fe''llar: parler, aimer, habiter, travailler — 80% fe''llar). Tuslanish qo''shimchalari: je -e, tu -es, il/elle -e, nous -ons, vous -ez, ils/elles -ent (oxirgi -ent talaffuz qilinmaydi! Parler: je parle, tu parles, il parle, nous parlons, vous parlez, ils parlent);
2) II guruh (-ir bilan tugovchi to''g''ri fe''llar: finir, choisir);
3) III guruh (noto''g''ri fe''llar: être, avoir, aller, faire, prendre).
Liaison (ulanish): so''z oxiridagi o''qilmaydigan undosh keyingi unli bilan boshlangan so''z bilan birikib o''qiladi (les amis -> le-zami).', '[{"title": "I guruh fe''lini tuslash", "problem": "''Habiter'' (yashamoq) fe''lini ''nous'' va ''ils'' shaxslarida tuslang.", "step_by_step": "O''zak: habit-.\nNous habitons (biz yashaymiz);\nIls habitent (ular yashaydilar — -ent o''qilmaydi).", "answer": "Nous habitons, ils habitent"}, {"title": "Être (bo''lmoq) fe''li hozirgi zamonda", "problem": "''Men talabaman'' va ''Biz do''stlarmiz'' jumlalarini yozing.", "step_by_step": "Être tuslanishi: je suis, tu es, il est, nous sommes, vous êtes, ils sont.\nNatija: ''Je suis étudiant'', ''Nous sommes amis''.", "answer": "Je suis étudiant, nous sommes amis"}]'::jsonb, '''Aimer'' (sevmoq/yoqtirmoq) fe''lini ''je'' olmoshi bilan qo''llang.', 'J''aime (unli bilan boshlangani uchun ''je'' dagi e tushib qoladi: J''aime).', '[{"question": "Fransuz tilida -er bilan tugaydigan fe''llar qaysi guruhga kiradi?", "options": ["I guruh", "II guruh", "III guruh", "Noto''g''ri guruh"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Fransuz tilidagi fe''llarning aksariyati -er bilan tugovchi I guruh muntazam fe''llaridir."}, {"question": "Ils/Elles shaxsida I guruh fe''llarining -ent qo''shimchasi qanday talaffuz qilinadi?", "options": ["-ent deb eshitiladi", "Umuman talaffuz qilinmaydi (o''qilmaydi)", "-on deb o''qiladi", "-e deb o''qiladi"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Uchinchi shaxs ko''plikdagi -ent fe''l qo''shimchasi o''qilmaydi (masalan: ils parlent talaffuzda ''il parl'')."}, {"question": "Unli bilan boshlangan so''zlar oldida ''le'' va ''la'' artikli qanday yoziladi?", "options": ["O''zgarmaydi", "l'' ko''rinishida apostrof bilan", "les bo''ladi", "tushib qoladi"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Eliziya (qisqarish) hodisasiga ko''ra unli oldida l'' yoziladi (l''ami, l''hôtel)."}]'::jsonb, '["fransuz tili", "artikl", "parler", "I guruh", "liaison", "A1", "6-sinf"]'::jsonb, 25) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
- ''Être'' yordamchi fe''li bilan: 14 ta asosiy harakat fe''li (aller, venir, arriver, partir, entrer, sortir, monter, descendre, naître, mourir...) va barcha o''zlik (pronominaux: se laver) fe''llari ishlatiladi. MUHIM: Être bilan kelganda Participe passé ega bilan jins va sonda moslashadi (Elle est allée — e qo''shiladi; Ils sont allés — s qo''shiladi);
- Qolgan barcha fe''llar ''avoir'' bilan ishlatiladi (moslashmaydi: J''ai mangé, elle a mangé).
Participe passé yasalishi: I guruh -er -> -é (parlé); II guruh -ir -> -i (fini); III guruh: fait, pris, vu, bu.
Futur Simple (Oddiy kelasi zamon): Infinitivga -ai, -as, -a, -ons, -ez, -ont qo''shimchalari qo''shiladi (je parlerai, tu parleras, nous parlerons).', '[{"title": "Passé Composé da moslashuv", "problem": "''Marie (aller) à Paris hier'' gapini Passé Composé da yozing.", "step_by_step": "1) Aller fe''li ''être'' bilan keladi: Marie est...\n2) Marie ayol jinsida bo''lgani uchun Participe passé ga -e qo''shiladi: allée.\nNatija: ''Marie est allée à Paris hier''.", "answer": "Marie est allée à Paris hier"}, {"title": "Futur Simple da jumlalar", "problem": "''Ertaga men yangi kitob o''qiyman'' jumlasini fransuzcha yozing (lire).", "step_by_step": "Demain, je lirai un nouveau livre (lire -> lir-ai).", "answer": "Demain, je lirai un nouveau livre"}]'::jsonb, 'Passé Composé ga aylantiring: ''Nous (finir) le travail'' (avoir bilan).', '''Nous avons fini le travail''.', '[{"question": "Passé Composé da ''aller'' (bormoq) fe''li qaysi yordamchi fe''l bilan ishlatiladi?", "options": ["avoir", "être", "faire", "aller"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Joy o''zgarishini bildiruvchi ''aller'' fe''li har doim ''être'' bilan tuslanadi."}, {"question": "''Être'' yordamchi fe''li bilan kelganda Participe passé nima bilan moslashadi?", "options": ["Obyekt bilan", "Eganing jinsi va soni bilan", "Moslashmaydi", "Vaqt bilan"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Être bilan kelganda ayol jinsi uchun -e, ko''plik uchun -s qo''shimchasi qo''shiladi."}, {"question": "Futur Simple kelasi zamoni odatda nimanining asosida yasaladi?", "options": ["Fe''l infinitiviga maxsus qo''shimchalar qo''shish orqali", "Hozirgi zamon orqali", "Avoir + V3", "Yordamchi fe''l bilan"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Futur Simple fe''lning to''liq infinitiviga -ai, -as, -a, -ons, -ez, -ont qo''shish orqali hosil qilinadi."}]'::jsonb, '["fransuz tili", "passé composé", "futur simple", "avoir être", "A2", "8-sinf"]'::jsonb, 30) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
- Present Simple -> Past Simple (am/is/are -> was/were, play -> played);
- Present Continuous -> Past Continuous (is playing -> was playing);
- Past Simple va Present Perfect -> Past Perfect (went/has gone -> had gone);
- Future Simple (will) -> Future-in-the-Past (would).
Ko''rsatkichlarning o''zgarishi: today -> that day, tomorrow -> the next day, yesterday -> the day before, now -> then, here -> there, this -> that. O''zbek tilida bunday majburiy zamon siljishi yo''q (''U ertaga kelishini aytdi'' — mazmun saqlanadi).', '[{"title": "Ko''chirma gapni o''zlashtirma gapga aylantirish", "problem": "Direct: Tom said: ''I am learning German now''. Ushbu gapni Indirect Speech ga o''tkazing.", "step_by_step": "1) Bosh gap: Tom said that...\n2) I -> he;\n3) am learning (Present Cont.) -> was learning (Past Cont.);\n4) now -> then.\nNatija: ''Tom said that he was learning German then''.", "answer": "Tom said that he was learning German then"}, {"title": "Kelasi zamonning o''zgarishi", "problem": "''She said: I will help you tomorrow'' gapini o''zlashtiring.", "step_by_step": "will -> would; tomorrow -> the next/following day.\nNatija: ''She said that she would help me the following day''.", "answer": "She said that she would help me the following day"}]'::jsonb, 'Indirect ga o''giring: ''He said: I have lost my keys''.', '''He said that he had lost his keys'' (have lost -> had lost).', '[{"question": "Bosh gap o''tgan zamonda bo''lsa, ''will'' yordamchi fe''li ko''chirma gapda nimaga aylanadi?", "options": ["shall", "would", "had been", "will be"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Zamonlar moslashuviga ko''ra ''will'' o''rniga ''would'' (Future-in-the-Past) qo''llanadi."}, {"question": "O''zlashtirma gapda ''yesterday'' so''zi nimaga o''zgaradi?", "options": ["tomorrow", "the day before (the previous day)", "that day", "now"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "''Yesterday'' o''rniga ''the day before'' yoki ''the previous day'' ishlatiladi."}, {"question": "Qaysi holatda zamonlar moslashuvi qoidasi qo''llanilmaydi va zamon o''zgarmaydi?", "options": ["Har doim o''zgaradi", "Tabiat qonuni va doimiy haqiqat ifodalanganda (''The teacher said that water boils at 100 C'')", "Faqat savollarda", "Inkor gaplarda"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Umumiy ilmiy haqiqatlar va tabiat qonunlari ifodalanganda zamon o''zgarmasdan Present Simple da qoladi."}]'::jsonb, '["chet tili", "reported speech", "sequence of tenses", "zamonlar moslashuvi", "B2", "11-sinf"]'::jsonb, 35) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
1) Inversion (Inversiya — so''z tartibining teskari aylanishi): Inkor yoki cheklovchi so''zlar gap boshiga chiqqanda yordamchi fe''l egadan oldinga o''tadi (so''roq gap shaklidek):
- Never, Rarely, Seldom, Barely, Scarcely, Little, Hardly... when, No sooner... than;
Masalan: ''I have never seen such beauty'' -> ''Never have I seen such beauty''; ''Hardly had he arrived when the rain started''.
- Only after / Not only... but also: ''Not only did he win, but he also broke the record''.
2) Cleft Sentences (Ajratilgan gaplar): Fikrning bir bo''lagiga alohida urg''u berish uchun ''It is / It was ... that / who'' yoki ''What ... is / was'' konstruksiyasi ishlatiladi:
- ''John broke the window yesterday'' -> ''It was John who broke the window'' (Aynan Jon sindirdi);
- ''I need a cup of hot coffee'' -> ''What I need is a cup of hot coffee''.', '[{"title": "Inversiya hosil qilish", "problem": "''He little knew about the upcoming danger'' gapini inversiya bilan qayta yozing.", "step_by_step": "''Little'' so''zini gap boshiga chiqaramiz. Knew (Past Simple) -> yordamchi fe''l ''did'':\nNatija: ''Little did he know about the upcoming danger''.", "answer": "Little did he know about the upcoming danger"}, {"title": "Cleft sentence tuzish", "problem": "''His kindness impressed me most'' gapiga ''What'' bilan boshlanuvchi cleft sentence tuzing.", "step_by_step": "Natija: ''What impressed me most was his kindness''.", "answer": "What impressed me most was his kindness"}]'::jsonb, 'Inversiyaga aylantiring: ''We had scarcely started the journey when the car broke down.''', '''Scarcely had we started the journey when the car broke down.''', '[{"question": "''Rarely'' so''zi gap boshida kelganda gap tuzilishi qanday bo''ladi?", "options": ["Oddiy darak gap tartibi saqlanadi", "Yordamchi fe''l egadan oldinga o''tadi (inversiya)", "Fe''l oxiriga suriladi", "Inkor yuklamasi qo''shiladi"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Inkor va cheklov ma''nosidagi ravishlar gap boshida kelganda inversiya (yordamchi fe''l + ega) talab qilinadi."}, {"question": "''No sooner had I closed my eyes ... the phone rang'' — nuqtalar o''rniga qaysi bog''lovchi qo''yiladi?", "options": ["when", "than", "then", "that"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "''No sooner ... than'' qat''iy korrelyativ juftlikdir (''Hardly ... when'' bilan adashtirmaslik kerak)."}, {"question": "Cleft sentences nima maqsadda qo''llaniladi?", "options": ["Faqat savol berish uchun", "Gapning ma''lum bir bo''lagiga kuchli urg''u va ta''kid berish uchun", "Matnni qisqartirish uchun", "Faqat o''tgan zamonda"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Cleft gaplar (masalan: It was Ali who...) aynan ma''lum shaxs yoki voqeani alohida ajratib ko''rsatish uchun ishlatiladi."}]'::jsonb, '["chet tili", "inversion", "cleft sentences", "advanced grammar", "C1", "11-sinf"]'::jsonb, 35) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
- SELECT: ma''lumotlarni tanlash (SELECT * FROM users WHERE age > 18);
- INSERT INTO: yangi ma''lumot qo''shish (INSERT INTO users (name, age) VALUES (''Ali'', 20));
- UPDATE: ma''lumotni tahrirlash (UPDATE users SET age = 21 WHERE id = 1);
- DELETE: ma''lumotni o''chirish (DELETE FROM users WHERE id = 5).', '[{"title": "SELECT so''rovi va filtrlash", "problem": "''Students'' jadvalidan bahosi 5 bo''lgan o''quvchilarning ismi va familiyasini saralangan holda tanlab oling.", "step_by_step": "SQL kodi:\nSELECT first_name, last_name \nFROM students \nWHERE grade = 5 \nORDER BY last_name ASC;", "answer": "SELECT first_name, last_name FROM students WHERE grade = 5 ORDER BY last_name ASC;"}, {"title": "Primary Key ahamiyati", "problem": "Nima sababdan odamning ism-familiyasi Primary Key qilib olinmaydi?", "step_by_step": "Chunki bir xil ism-familiyali odamlar juda ko''p uchraydi. Primary Key esa mutlaqo takrorlanmas (unikal) bo''lishi shart, shu bois unikal raqamli ID ishlatiladi.", "answer": "Ism takrorlanishi mumkin, Primary Key esa mutlaqo unikal bo''lishi shart"}]'::jsonb, '''Users'' jadvalidan ''status'' ustuni ''banned'' bo''lgan barcha yozuvlarni o''chiruvchi SQL so''rovini yozing.', 'DELETE FROM users WHERE status = ''banned'';', '[{"question": "Jadvaldagi har bir yozuvni unikal ajratib turuvchi kalit nima deyiladi?", "options": ["Foreign Key", "Primary Key", "Index Key", "Super Key"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Primary Key (birlamchi kalit) yozuvning yagona unikal identifikatoridir."}, {"question": "Ma''lumotlar bazasidan ma''lumotlarni o''qib olish (tanlash) uchun qaysi SQL buyrug''i ishlatiladi?", "options": ["GET", "READ", "SELECT", "FETCH"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "SELECT ma''lumotlarni qidirish va olish uchun standart SQL komandasidir."}, {"question": "Ikkita jadval orasidagi aloqani bog''lovchi kalit nima deyiladi?", "options": ["Primary Key", "Foreign Key (tashqi kalit)", "Unique Key", "Check Key"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Foreign Key bir jadval ustunini ikkinchi jadvaldagi Primary Key ga bog''laydi."}]'::jsonb, '["informatika", "ma''lumotlar bazasi", "SQL", "select", "primary key", "database", "9-sinf"]'::jsonb, 35) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
- Enkapsulyatsiya (Encapsulation): ma''lumotlar (maydonlar) va ularni boshqaruvchi metodlarni bitta sinf ichida birlashtirish hamda tashqi xavfli aralashuvdan yashirish (private, protected, public);
- Vorislik (Inheritance): mavjud sinf xossalarini yangi sinfga meros qilib o''tkazish (masalan, Animal -> Dog);
- Polimorfizm (Polymorphism): bir xil nomdagi metodlarning har xil sinflarda turlicha xatti-harakat qilishi (masalan, Dog.sound() -> ''Vov'', Cat.sound() -> ''Miyov'');
- Abstraksiya (Abstraction): faqat muhim xususiyatlarni ko''rsatib, ichki murakkab detallarni yashirish (interface, abstract class).', '[{"title": "OOP vorisligi misoli (Python)", "problem": "Animal umumiy sinfidan Dog sinfini meros qilib oling.", "step_by_step": "class Animal:\n    def __init__(self, name):\n        self.name = name\n    def speak(self):\n        pass\n\nclass Dog(Animal):\n    def speak(self):\n        return f''{self.name} vovulladi!''\n\ndog = Dog(''Bobik'')\nprint(dog.speak())", "answer": "Bobik vovulladi!"}, {"title": "Enkapsulyatsiya va ma''lumotlarni himoyalash", "problem": "Bank hisob raqamidagi balansni to''g''ridan-to''g''ri o''zgartirishdan qanday himoya qilinadi?", "step_by_step": "Balans o''zgaruvchisi private (__balance) qilinadi. Unga faqat maxsus deposit() va withdraw() metodlari orqali, qat''iy tekshiruvdan so''ng qiymat kiritishga ruxsat beriladi.", "answer": "Private maydonlar va getter/setter metodlari orqali"}]'::jsonb, 'Polimorfizm nima uchun kodni kengaytirishda qulaylik yaratadi?', 'Yangi sinflar qo''shilganda asosiy dastur kodini o''zgartirmasdan, umumiy interfeys orqali barcha obyektlarni bir xilda boshqarish imkonini beradi.', '[{"question": "OOP ning qaysi ustuni ichki murakkablikni yashirib, faqat zarur interfeysni taqdim etadi?", "options": ["Vorislik", "Abstraksiya", "Polimorfizm", "Sikl"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Abstraksiya foydalanuvchiga faqat kerakli tugmalarni ko''rsatib, ichki murakkab ishlash mexanizmini yashiradi."}, {"question": "Sinf (Class) va Obyekt (Object) orasidagi farq nima?", "options": ["Hech qanday farq yo''q", "Sinf — chizma/qolip, obyekt esa shu qolip asosida xotirada yaratilgan aniq nusxadir", "Obyekt faqat bitta bo''ladi", "Sinf ma''lumot saqlamaydi"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Sinf barcha nusxalar uchun umumiy reja, obyekt esa o''sha rejadan yaratilgan real narsadir."}, {"question": "Meros olish (Inheritance) nima maqsadda ishlatiladi?", "options": ["Dasturni sekinlashtirish uchun", "Kodni qayta yozmasdan (reusability) kengaytirish uchun", "Faqat xotirani tejash uchun", "Boshqa tildan kod ko''chirish uchun"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Vorislik kodni qayta ishlatish (DRY - Don''t Repeat Yourself) imkonini beradi."}]'::jsonb, '["dasturlash", "OOP", "enkapsulyatsiya", "vorislik", "polimorfizm", "abstraksiya", "universitet"]'::jsonb, 35) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
1) Massiv (Array) — xotirada ketma-ket joylashgan, bir xil turdagi elementlar to''plami. Indeks orqali murojaat o''ta tez: O(1), lekin o''rtasiga element qo''shish O(n) vaqt oladi;
2) Bog''langan ro''yxat (Linked List) — har bir tugun (node) qiymat va keyingi tugunga ko''rsatkich (pointer) saqlaydi. Xotirada tarqoq joylashishi mumkin, element qo''shish oson;
3) Stack (Stek) — LIFO (Last In, First Out — ''Oxirgi kirgan — birinchi chiqadi'') tamoyilida ishlaydi. Amallar: push() — qo''shish, pop() — oxirgisini olish. Misol: brauzerdagi ''Back'' (orqaga) tugmasi, matn muharriridagi Undo (bekor qilish), funksiyalar chaqiruv steki;
4) Queue (Navbat) — FIFO (First In, First Out — ''Birinchi kirgan — birinchi chiqadi'') tamoyili. Amallar: enqueue() — navbatga qo''shish, dequeue() — navbatdan chiqarish. Misol: printerdagi hujjatlar navbati, serverga kelgan so''rovlar navbati.', '[{"title": "Stack (LIFO) amali", "problem": "Bo''sh stekkaga ketma-ket push(10), push(20), push(30) amallari bajarildi. So''ngra pop() amali chaqirilsa qaysi son qaytadi?", "step_by_step": "Stekkaga eng oxirgi kirgan element 30 bo''lgani uchun LIFO qoidasiga ko''ra pop() amali aynan 30 sonini olib tashlaydi va qaytaradi.", "answer": "30"}, {"title": "Queue (FIFO) amali", "problem": "Bo''sh navbatga enqueue(''Ali''), enqueue(''Vali'') qo''shildi. Birinchi bo''lib dequeue() chaqirilsa kim chiqadi?", "step_by_step": "Navbatga birinchi bo''lib ''Ali'' kelgan (FIFO), shuning uchun birinchi bo''lib ''Ali'' xizmat olib chiqadi.", "answer": "Ali"}]'::jsonb, 'Qavslarning to''g''ri yopilganligini (masalan: ''({[]})'') tekshirish uchun qaysi ma''lumotlar tuzilmasidan foydalanish eng qulay?', 'Stack (stek) tuzilmasi eng qulay: ochiq qavslar stekkaga kiritiladi, yopiq qavs kelganda stekkadan mos ochuvchi qavs bilan juftligi tekshirilib pop() qilinadi.', '[{"question": "LIFO (Last In, First Out) tamoyili asosida ishlovchi ma''lumotlar tuzilmasi qaysi?", "options": ["Queue (Navbat)", "Stack (Stek)", "Massiv", "Daraxt (Tree)"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Stek — oxirgi kiritilgan elementni birinchi bo''lib chiqaruvchi LIFO tizimidir."}, {"question": "FIFO (First In, First Out) tamoyili qaysi tizimga xos?", "options": ["Stack", "Queue (Navbat)", "Graph", "HashTable"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Navbat (Queue) har doim birinchi kelgan elementga birinchi xizmat ko''rsatish qoidasida ishlaydi."}, {"question": "Massivda n-indeksdagi elementni olish amali qanday vaqt murakkabligiga ega?", "options": ["O(1) doimiy vaqt", "O(n) chiziqli vaqt", "O(log n)", "O(n^2)"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Xotira manzili to''g''ridan-to''g''ri hisoblangani sababli massiv elementiga indeks orqali O(1) vaqtda murojaat qilinadi."}]'::jsonb, '["dasturlash", "ma''lumotlar tuzilmasi", "stack", "queue", "massiv", "LIFO", "FIFO"]'::jsonb, 35) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
- O(1) — doimiy vaqt (eng tez);
- O(log n) — logarifmik vaqt (juda samarali, masalan, Binary Search);
- O(n) — chiziqli vaqt (Linear Search);
- O(n log n) — optimal saralash (QuickSort, MergeSort);
- O(n^2) — kvadratik vaqt (Bubble Sort, Selection Sort).
Qidirish algoritmlari:
1) Linear Search (Chiziqli qidirish) — elementlarni boshidan oxirigacha bittalab tekshiradi, O(n);
2) Binary Search (Ikkilik qidirish) — FAQAT saralangan massivda ishlaydi. Har bir qadamda massivni teng ikkiga bo''ladi, O(log n).
Saralash algoritmlari:
1) Bubble Sort (Pufaksimon saralash) — qo''shni elementlarni solishtirib o''rnini almashtiradi, O(n^2);
2) QuickSort (Tezkor saralash) — tayanch element (pivot) tanlanadi, undan kichiklar chapga, kattalar o''ngga ajratiladi va rekursiv saralanadi, o''rtacha O(n log n).', '[{"title": "Binary Search samaradorligi", "problem": "1 000 000 (bir million) ta saralangan elementdan iborat massivda qidirilayotgan sonni topish uchun Binary Search eng ko''pi bilan necha qadam sarflaydi?", "step_by_step": "Har qadamda massiv teng ikkiga bo''linadi: 2^x >= 1 000 000. 2^20 = 1 048 576. Demak, eng ko''pi bilan atigi 20 ta taqqoslash kifoya (chiziqli qidiruv esa 1 million qadam sarflashi mumkin edi).", "answer": "Eng ko''pi bilan 20 ta qadam"}, {"title": "Big O taqqoslash", "problem": "1000 ta element uchun O(n^2) va O(n log n) algoritmlari taxminan nechtadan amal bajaradi?", "step_by_step": "1) O(n^2): 1000^2 = 1 000 000 (bir million amal);\n2) O(n log n): 1000 * log2(1000) ~ 1000 * 10 = 10 000 amal (100 marta tezroq!).", "answer": "O(n^2) ~ 1 000 000 amal, O(n log n) ~ 10 000 amal"}]'::jsonb, 'Binary Search algoritmini qo''llashning eng asosiy zaruriy sharti nima?', 'Massiv elementlari oldindan o''sish yoki kamayish tartibida qat''iy saralangan (sorted) bo''lishi shart.', '[{"question": "Saralangan massivda qidirish uchun eng tezkor algoritm qaysi?", "options": ["Linear Search", "Binary Search (Ikkilik qidirish)", "Bubble Search", "Brute Force"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Binary Search O(log n) vaqt murakkabligi bilan eng samarali qidirish algoritmidir."}, {"question": "QuickSort algoritmining o''rtacha vaqt murakkabligi qanday?", "options": ["O(n^2)", "O(n log n)", "O(1)", "O(n)"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "QuickSort va MergeSort ning o''rtacha samaradorligi O(n log n) ga teng."}, {"question": "Big O notatsiyasida eng sekin (eng yomon) o''sish darajasi qaysi?", "options": ["O(1)", "O(log n)", "O(n)", "O(2^n) eksponensial"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "Eksponensial O(2^n) va faktorial O(n!) eng og''ir va qiyin murakkablik hisoblanadi."}]'::jsonb, '["dasturlash", "algoritmlar", "big O", "binary search", "quicksort", "murakkablik"]'::jsonb, 35) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
1) S — Single Responsibility Principle (SRP): Har bir sinf faqat bitta vazifani bajarishi va uni o''zgartirish uchun faqat bitta sabab bo''lishi kerak;
2) O — Open/Closed Principle (OCP): Dasturiy ta''minot kengayish uchun ochiq, o''zgartirish uchun yopiq bo''lishi kerak (yangi funksiya qo''shganda eski kodni buzmaslik);
3) L — Liskov Substitution Principle (LSP): Voris sinflar asosiy ota sinf o''rnida uning xatti-harakatini buzmasdan bemalol ishlay olishi lozim;
4) I — Interface Segregation Principle (ISP): Bitta katta, og''ir interfeysdan ko''ra bir nechta kichik, maxsus interfeyslar yaratish afzal;
5) D — Dependency Inversion Principle (DIP): Yuqori darajali modullar quyi darajali modullarga to''g''ridan-to''g''ri bog''liq bo''lmasligi, ikkalasi ham abstraksiyalarga bog''lanishi kerak.
Clean Code: o''zgaruvchilarga mazmunli nom berish, ortiqcha izohlardan qochish, funksiyalar kichik bo''lishi va faqat 1 ishni qilishi kerak.', '[{"title": "Single Responsibility (Yagona javobgarlik) buzilishi", "problem": "''User'' sinfi ham foydalanuvchi ma''lumotlarini saqlasa, ham uni bazaga yozsa, ham email xabar yuborsa, bu to''g''rimi?", "step_by_step": "Bu SRP prinsipining qo''pol buzilishidir. Buni 3 ga ajratish kerak: 1) User (ma''lumot modeli); 2) UserRepository (bazaga yozuvchi); 3) EmailService (xat yuboruvchi).", "answer": "Xato. Vazifalar alohida sinflarga ajratilishi shart (SRP)"}, {"title": "Open/Closed tamoyilini qo''llash", "problem": "Yangi to''lov tizimini (masalan, Payme, Click, Uzum) qo''shganda asosiy kodni buzmaslik uchun nima qilinadi?", "step_by_step": "Umumiy ''PaymentProcessor'' interfeysi yaratiladi. Har bir yangi tizim shu interfeysni amalga oshiradi (implements). Asosiy kod esa yangi sinfni to''g''ridan-to''g''ri qabul qilaveradi (kod kengayadi, lekin o''zgarmaydi).", "answer": "Interfeys va polimorfizm orqali kengaytiriladi"}]'::jsonb, 'DRY (Don''t Repeat Yourself) va KISS (Keep It Simple, Stupid) qoidalarining ma''nosi nima?', 'DRY — kodni takrorlamaslik, umumiy funksiyalarga chiqarish; KISS — kodni keraksiz darajada murakkablashtirmasdan, imkon qadar sodda va tushunarli yozish.', '[{"question": "SOLID qoidalaridagi ''S'' harfi nimani bildiradi?", "options": ["Security Principle", "Single Responsibility Principle (Yagona javobgarlik)", "Speed Principle", "Simple Code"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Single Responsibility — sinf faqat bitta vazifaga javobgar bo''lishi tamoyili."}, {"question": "Open/Closed prinsipi dastur kodiga nisbatan qanday talab qo''yadi?", "options": ["Kodni hech qachon ochmaslik", "Kengayish uchun ochiq, o''zgartirish uchun yopiq bo''lishi kerak", "Faqat ochiq kodli (open source) bo''lishi kerak", "Faqat yopiq sinflar bilan ishlash"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Yangi imkoniyatlarni eski kodni buzmasdan yangi modullar qo''shish orqali kiritish talab qilinadi."}, {"question": "Clean Code bo''yicha yaxshi funksiya qanday bo''lishi kerak?", "options": ["Kamida 100 qator bo''lishi", "Kichik bo''lib, faqat bitta vazifani a''lo darajada bajarishi kerak", "Barcha parametrlarni bitta funksiyaga yig''ish", "Ko''p vazifali bo''lishi"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Yaxshi funksiya kichik va bitta aniq ishni bajaruvchi bo''lishi shart."}]'::jsonb, '["dasturlash", "arxitektura", "SOLID", "clean code", "refactoring", "universitet"]'::jsonb, 35) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
- GET: ma''lumotlarni olish (/api/courses);
- POST: yangi ma''lumot yaratish (/api/courses);
- PUT / PATCH: mavjud ma''lumotni yangilash (/api/courses/12);
- DELETE: ma''lumotni o''chirish (/api/courses/12).
Status kodlar: 200 (OK), 201 (Created), 400 (Bad Request), 401 (Unauthorized), 404 (Not Found), 500 (Internal Server Error).', '[{"title": "Oddiy Express.js GET marshruti", "problem": "Barcha fanlar ro''yxatini qaytaruvchi oddiy Express.js API yo''lini yozing.", "step_by_step": "const express = require(''express'');\nconst app = express();\n\nconst subjects = [\n  { id: 1, name: ''Matematika'' },\n  { id: 2, name: ''Fizika'' }\n];\n\napp.get(''/api/subjects'', (req, res) => {\n  res.status(200).json(subjects);\n});\n\napp.listen(3000, () => console.log(''Server 3000-portda ishlamoqda''));", "answer": "app.get(''/api/subjects'', ...)"}, {"title": "HTTP status kodlar", "problem": "Foydalanuvchi so''ragan material bazada topilmasa, server qanday HTTP kod qaytarishi kerak?", "step_by_step": "Resurs topilmaganda har doim 404 (Not Found) kodi qaytariladi. Agar server xatosi bo''lsa 500 bo''lardi.", "answer": "404 Not Found"}]'::jsonb, 'Yangi material yaratish uchun mijoz serverga qaysi HTTP metodida va qanday formatda so''rov yuboradi?', 'POST metodida va so''rov tanasida (request body) JSON formatida ma''lumot yuboradi.', '[{"question": "REST API da yangi resurs yaratish uchun qaysi HTTP metodi ishlatiladi?", "options": ["GET", "POST", "PUT", "DELETE"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "POST metodi serverda yangi yozuv yaratish uchun xizmat qiladi."}, {"question": "So''rov muvaffaqiyatli bajarilganini bildiruvchi standart HTTP kodi qaysi?", "options": ["200 OK", "404 Not Found", "500 Server Error", "301 Redirect"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "200 kodi so''rov muvaffaqiyatli bajarilganini bildiradi."}, {"question": "Node.js nima uchun yuqori yuklamalarda ham tez ishlaydi?", "options": ["Ko''p oqimli bo''lgani uchun", "Asinxron va bloklamaydigan (non-blocking I/O) Event Loop modeli hisobiga", "Faqat kichik dasturlar uchun", "C++ da yozilgani uchun"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Node.js asinxron Event Loop yordamida minglab so''rovlarni bitta oqimda to''xtab qolmasdan qayta ishlaydi."}]'::jsonb, '["web development", "backend", "node.js", "express", "REST API", "HTTP"]'::jsonb, 35) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
1) List (ro''yxat: [1, 2, 3]) — tartiblangan, o''zgaruvchan (mutable), dublikatlarga ruxsat beradi;
2) Tuple (kortej: (1, 2, 3)) — tartiblangan, o''zgarmas (immutable — o''zgartirib bo''lmaydi);
3) Set (to''plam: {1, 2, 3}) — tartiblanmagan, faqat unikal (takrorlanmas) elementlarni saqlaydi;
4) Dictionary (lug''at: {''ism'': ''Ali'', ''yosh'': 20}) — kalit-qiymat (key-value) juftliklari, kalitlar unikal bo''ladi. Pythonda bloklar qavslar bilan emas, balki qat''iy surilishlar (indentation — 4 ta bo''shliq) bilan belgilanadi.', '[{"title": "Lug''at (Dictionary) bilan ishlash", "problem": "Talabaning baholari lug''atidan o''rtacha ballni hisoblang.", "step_by_step": "grades = {''matematika'': 5, ''fizika'': 4, ''ona_tili'': 5}\naverage = sum(grades.values()) / len(grades)\n# sum = 14, len = 3 -> 14 / 3 = 4.67\nprint(round(average, 2))", "answer": "4.67"}, {"title": "Ro''yxatdan dublikatlarni tozalash", "problem": "numbers = [1, 2, 2, 3, 4, 4, 5] ro''yxatidagi takrorlarni qanday olib tashlash mumkin?", "step_by_step": "Ro''yxatni Set ga aylantiramiz, set faqat unikal qiymat saqlaydi: unique_numbers = list(set(numbers)). Natija: [1, 2, 3, 4, 5].", "answer": "list(set(numbers))"}]'::jsonb, 'List comprehension yordamida 1 dan 10 gacha bo''lgan sonlarning kvadratlari ro''yxatini 1 qatorda hosil qiling.', 'squares = [x**2 for x in range(1, 11)]', '[{"question": "Pythonda elementlarini o''zgartirib bo''lmaydigan (immutable) to''plam qaysi?", "options": ["List (ro''yxat)", "Tuple (kortej)", "Dictionary (lug''at)", "Set"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Tuple bir marta yaratilgach, unga element qo''shish yoki o''chirish mumkin emas."}, {"question": "Pythonda kod bloklari (if, for, funksiyalar) qanday ajratiladi?", "options": ["Jingalak qavslar { } bilan", "begin ... end bilan", "Surilishlar (indentation / bo''shliqlar) bilan", "Nuqtali vergul bilan"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "Python sintaksisining asosiy belgisi — qat''iy bo''shliqlar (indentation) tizimidir."}, {"question": "Kalit-qiymat (key-value) juftligi asosida ishlovchi ma''lumot turi nima?", "options": ["List", "Tuple", "Dictionary", "Float"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "Dictionary (dict) kalit bo''yicha qiymat saqlovchi ma''lumotlar tuzilmasidir."}]'::jsonb, '["python", "dasturlash", "list", "dict", "tuple", "sintaksis"]'::jsonb, 30) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
    if n <= 1:
        return 1
    return n * factorial(n - 1)', '[{"question": "Fayllar bilan ishlashda ''with open(...)'' nima sababdan afzal?", "options": ["Faylni shifrlaydi", "Amal tugagach faylni avtomatik va xavfsiz yopadi", "Faylni o''chiradi", "Faqat tezlik uchun"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "''with'' kontekst menejeri bo''lib, xatolik yuz berganda ham faylni to''g''ri yopishni kafolatlaydi."}, {"question": "Ixtiyoriy sondagi pozitsion argumentlarni qabul qilish uchun nima ishlatiladi?", "options": ["*args", "**kwargs", "&args", "lambda"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "*args funksiyaga istalgancha argumentlarni tuple sifatida uzatish imkonini beradi."}, {"question": "Nolga bo''lish paytida qaysi standart Python xatosi (Exception) yuzaga keladi?", "options": ["ValueError", "TypeError", "ZeroDivisionError", "IndexError"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "Nolga bo''lishga uringanda ZeroDivisionError xatosi yuzaga keladi."}]'::jsonb, '["python", "funksiyalar", "fayllar", "try-except", "json", "lambda"]'::jsonb, 35) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
- Simmetrik shifrlash (AES): bitta maxfiy kalit bilan shifrlanadi va ochiladi (juda tez, katta hajmlar uchun);
- Asimmetrik shifrlash (RSA): ikkita kalit ishlatiladi — ochiq kalit (Public key — hamma ko''radi, faqat shifrlaydi) va yopiq kalit (Private key — faqat egasida saqlanadi, shifrni ochadi). Raqamli imzo (Digital Signature) — xat jo''natuvchining shaxsini va hujjat o''zgarmaganini isbotlaydi. Tarmoq xavfsizligi: Firewall (Xavfsizlik devori) tarmoq trafigini filtrlaydi; VPN (Virtual Private Network) shifrlangan xavfsiz tunnel yaratadi.', '[{"title": "Asimmetrik shifrlash ishlashi", "problem": "Ali Valiga maxfiy xabar yubormoqchi. U xabarni kimning qaysi kaliti bilan shifrlashi kerak?", "step_by_step": "1) Ali Valining Ochiq kalitini (Public key) oladi;\n2) Xabarni Valining ochiq kaliti bilan shifrlaydi;\n3) Bu shifrni faqat Valining o''zidagina bor bo''lgan Yopiq kalit (Private key) ochishi mumkin.", "answer": "Valining ochiq kaliti (Public key) bilan shifrlaydi"}, {"title": "DDoS hujumi nima?", "problem": "DDoS (Distributed Denial of Service) hujumi qanday amalga oshiriladi va u CIA ning qaysi bo''g''inini buzadi?", "step_by_step": "Xakerlar minglab zararlangan botnet kompyuterlaridan serverga bir vaqtda millionlab soxta so''rovlar yuboradi. Server bardosh bera olmay o''chadi. Bu CIA ning Availability (Foydalanish imkoniyati) bo''g''inini buzadi.", "answer": "Serverni ortiqcha yuklama bilan qulatadi; Availability buziladi"}]'::jsonb, 'SHA-256 xesh funksiyasining qaytmaslik (bir tomonlama) xossasi nimani anglatadi?', 'Berilgan xesh kodidan (masalan, e3b0c442...) dastlabki matnni qaytarib tiklash matematik jihatdan imkonsiz ekanligini anglatadi.', '[{"question": "CIA xavfsizlik modelining 3 ta komponenti qaysi?", "options": ["Code, Internet, Access", "Confidentiality, Integrity, Availability", "CPU, IP, Antivirus", "Control, Identity, Audit"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Maxfiylik (Confidentiality), Yaxlitlik (Integrity) va Foydalanish imkoniyati (Availability) axborot xavfsizligi asosidir."}, {"question": "Asimmetrik kriptografiyada (masalan RSA) nechta kalitdan foydalaniladi?", "options": ["1 ta umumiy kalit", "2 ta kalit (Ochiq va Yopiq kalit juftligi)", "3 ta kalit", "Kalitsiz"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Asimmetrik shifrlash Public va Private key juftligi orqali ishlaydi."}, {"question": "Tarmoq paketlarini qoidalarga asosan tekshirib, ruxsatsiz ulanishlarni to''suvchi dastur yoki qurilma nima deyiladi?", "options": ["Router", "Firewall (Xavfsizlik devori)", "Switch", "Modem"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Firewall tarmoq trafigini tahlil qilib xavfli kirishlarni to''xtatadi."}]'::jsonb, '["kiberxavfsizlik", "kriptografiya", "RSA", "CIA triadasi", "firewall", "universitet"]'::jsonb, 35) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
1) Markaziy tendensiya o''lchovlari: O''rta arifmetik (Mean — barcha qiymatlar yig''indisi / soni); Mediana (Median — tartiblangan qatorning qoq o''rtasidagi qiymat, anomaliyalarga chidamli); Moda (Mode — eng ko''p takrorlangan qiymat);
2) Tarqoqlik o''lchovlari: Qamrov (Range = Max - Min); Dispersiya (Variance, sigma^2 — qiymatlarning o''rtachadan chetlanishlari kvadratlarining o''rtachasi); O''rtacha kvadratik chetlanish (Standard Deviation, sigma = sqrt(dispersiya));
3) Normal taqsimot (Gauss qo''ng''irog''i): tabiat va jamiyatdagi ko''plab tasodifiy miqdorlar qo''ng''iroqsimon simmetrik egri chiziq bo''ylab taqsimlanadi. ''Uch sigma'' qoidasi (68-95-99.7%): barcha qiymatlarning ~68% i mu +- 1*sigma oraliqda, ~95% i mu +- 2*sigma oraliqda, ~99.7% i mu +- 3*sigma oraliqda yotadi.', '[{"title": "Mediana va o''rtacha qiymat farqi", "problem": "Kompaniyada 4 nafar ishchi 3 mln so''mdan, 1 nafar rahbar 48 mln so''m maosh oladi. O''rtacha maosh va medianani toping.", "step_by_step": "1) O''rtacha maosh = (3*4 + 48) / 5 = 60 / 5 = 12 million so''m;\n2) Qator: 3, 3, 3, 3, 48. Qoq o''rtadagi son (Mediana) = 3 million so''m.\nAnomaliya (rahbar maoshi) tufayli o''rtacha ko''rsatkich buzilgan, mediana esa haqiqiy holatni (3 mln) aks ettiradi.", "answer": "O''rtacha: 12 mln, Mediana: 3 mln"}, {"title": "Standart chetlanish hisobi", "problem": "Sonlar: 2, 4, 6. O''rtacha kvadratik chetlanishni (sigma) toping.", "step_by_step": "1) O''rtacha = (2+4+6)/3 = 4;\n2) Kvadratlar ayirmasi: (2-4)^2 + (4-4)^2 + (6-4)^2 = 4 + 0 + 4 = 8;\n3) Dispersiya = 8 / 3 = 2.67;\n4) Standart chetlanish sigma = sqrt(2.67) ~ 1.63.", "answer": "sigma ~ 1.63"}]'::jsonb, 'Normal taqsimotda ma''lumotlarning taxminan necha foizi o''rtacha qiymatdan ikkita standart chetlanish (mu +- 2*sigma) oralig''iga to''g''ri keladi?', 'Taqsimot qoidasiga ko''ra taxminan 95.4% ma''lumotlar mu +- 2*sigma oralig''ida yotadi.', '[{"question": "Anomaliyalarga (outliers) nisbatan eng chidamli markaziy ko''rsatkich qaysi?", "options": ["O''rta arifmetik", "Mediana", "Dispersiya", "Standart chetlanish"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Mediana o''rtadagi tartib bo''yicha aniqlangani sababli chekka haddan tashqari katta/kichik sonlarga ta''sirlanmaydi."}, {"question": "Standart chetlanish (sigma) nimani ko''rsatadi?", "options": ["Eng katta sonni", "Ma''lumotlarning o''rtacha qiymat atrofida qanchalik tarqoq yoki zich joylashganligini", "Qatordagi elementlar sonini", "Foydani"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Standart chetlanish ma''lumotlar tarqoqligi va tebranish ko''lamini ifodalaydi."}, {"question": "Eng ko''p takrorlangan qiymat nima deyiladi?", "options": ["Mediana", "Moda", "Kvantil", "Gistogramma"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Moda — qatorda eng yuqori chastota bilan uchraydigan qiymatdir."}]'::jsonb, '["statistika", "mediana", "o''rtacha arifmetik", "dispersiya", "normal taqsimot", "universitet"]'::jsonb, 35) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
1) NPV (Net Present Value — Sof joriy qiymat): Kutilayotgan barcha diskontlangan pul tushumlari yig''indisi minus boshlang''ich investitsiya: NPV = Sum[CF_t / (1 + r)^t] - C_0. Qoida: Agar NPV > 0 bo''lsa, loyiha foydali va qabul qilinadi; NPV < 0 bo''lsa, loyiha rad etiladi;
2) IRR (Internal Rate of Return — Ichki daromadlilik stavkasi): NPV ni roppa-rosa nolga aylantiradigan diskont stavkasidir. Agar IRR kapital narxidan (WACC) yuqori bo''lsa loyiha qabul qilinadi.', '[{"title": "Kelajakdagi pulning bugungi qiymatini (PV) topish", "problem": "Agar diskont stavkasi r = 10% bo''lsa, 1 yildan keyin olinadigan 110 000 000 so''m pulning bugungi qiymati (PV) qancha?", "step_by_step": "PV = FV / (1 + r)^1 = 110 000 000 / (1 + 0.10) = 110 000 000 / 1.1 = 100 000 000 so''m.", "answer": "100 000 000 so''m"}, {"title": "NPV bo''yicha qaror qabul qilish", "problem": "Loyiha uchun 50 000 dollar tikiladi. Kutilayotgan pul tushumlarining joriy qiymati 65 000 dollar bo''lsa, loyiha qabul qilinadimi?", "step_by_step": "NPV = 65 000 - 50 000 = +15 000 dollar. NPV > 0 bo''lgani sababli kompaniya qiymati 15 000 dollarga oshadi, loyiha qabul qilinadi.", "answer": "NPV = +15 000 $ (Loyiha qabul qilinadi)"}]'::jsonb, 'Agar ikkita o''zaro bir-birini inkor qiluvchi loyiha taqdim etilsa va A loyihaning NPV si 50 000 $, B loyihaniki 35 000 $ bo''lsa, qaysi biri tanlanadi?', 'NPV qoidasiga ko''ra aksiyadorlar boyligini ko''proq oshiradigan A loyihasi (NPV = 50 000 $) tanlanadi.', '[{"question": "Investitsiya loyihasini qabul qilish uchun uning NPV ko''rsatkichi qanday bo''lishi shart?", "options": ["NPV < 0", "NPV = 0", "NPV > 0 (musbat)", "Manfiy"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "NPV > 0 bo''lgandagina loyiha barcha xarajatlarni qoplab, kompaniyaga sof foyda keltiradi."}, {"question": "Kelajakdagi kutilayotgan pul oqimlarini bugungi qiymatga keltirish jarayoni nima deyiladi?", "options": ["Inflyatsiya", "Diskontlash", "Kompaunding", "Amortizatsiya"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Diskontlash (Discounting) kelajakdagi pul qiymatini vaqt va xavf omilini hisobga olib bugungi kunga kamaytirishdir."}, {"question": "NPV ni roppa-rosa nolga tenglashtiruvchi foiz stavkasi nima deb ataladi?", "options": ["WACC", "IRR (Internal Rate of Return)", "ROI", "EBITDA"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "IRR loyihaning ichki rentabellik chegarasi bo''lib, unda NPV = 0 bo''ladi."}]'::jsonb, '["moliya", "korporativ moliya", "NPV", "IRR", "diskontlash", "TVM", "investitsiya", "universitet"]'::jsonb, 35) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
1) Tushuncha — narsa va hodisalarning eng muhim xossalarini umumlashtirib ifodalash (masalan, ''talaba'', ''uchburchak'');
2) Hukm — biror narsa haqida biror narsani tasdiqlovchi yoki inkor etuvchi fikr (''Oltin metalldir'' — rost hukm, ''Oy quyoshdan katta'' — yolg''on hukm);
3) Xulosa chiqarish (Sillogizm) — bir yoki bir nechta boshlang''ich hukmlardan (asoslardan) yangi hukm hosil qilish (Masalan: Barcha insonlar foniydir -> Suqrot insondir -> Demak, Suqrot foniydir).
4 ta asosiy mantiqiy qonun:
1) Ayniyat qonuni (A = A): fikr yuritish jarayonida har bir tushuncha o''z ma''nosida qat''iy saqlanishi kerak;
2) Ziddiyatsizlik qonuni: Ikkita bir-biriga zid hukm bir vaqtda va bitta nisbatda birdek rost bo''la olmaydi;
3) Uchinchisi istisno qonuni: Zid hukmlardan biri albatta rost, ikkinchisi yolg''on bo''ladi, uchinchi oraliq hukm bo''lishi mumkin emas;
4) Yetarli asos qonuni (Leybnits): Har qanday to''g''ri fikr yetarli dalillar bilan asoslangan bo''lishi shart.', '[{"title": "Deduksiya va Induksiya", "problem": "Deduktiv va Induktiv xulosa chiqarishning farqi nimada?", "step_by_step": "Deduksiya — umumiy qoidadan xususiy holatga xulosa chiqarish (Barcha metallar elektr o''tkazadi -> Temir metall -> Temir elektr o''tkazadi);\nInduksiya — xususiy misollardan umumiy xulosaga borish (Temir o''tkazadi, mis o''tkazadi, oltin o''tkazadi -> Barcha metallar elektr o''tkazar ekan).", "answer": "Deduksiya: umumiydan xususiyga; Induksiya: xususiydan umumiyga"}, {"title": "Mantiqiy xatoni aniqlash (Sofizm)", "problem": "''Nimaniki yo''qotmagan bo''lsang, o''sha narsa senda bor. Sen shoxlaringni yo''qotmading. Demak, sening shoxlaring bor''. Bu xulosada qaysi mantiqiy qonun buzilgan?", "step_by_step": "Bu yerda Ayniyat qonuni buzilgan. ''Yo''qotmagan narsa'' tushunchasi dastlab inson mulkida bo''lgan narsalar haqida, keyin esa umuman bo''lmagan narsa haqida turlicha ma''noda ishlatilib, so''z o''yini (sofizm) qilingan.", "answer": "Ayniyat qonuni buzilgan (so''z o''yini va soxta asos)"}]'::jsonb, 'Arastu yaratgan deduktiv xulosa chiqarish shakli (Sillogizm) nimalardan tashkil topgan?', 'Katta asos (umumiy qoida), kichik asos (xususiy fakt) va ulardan kelib chiquvchi yakuniy Xulosadan tashkil topgan.', '[{"question": "Mantiq ilmining asoschisi deb qaysi antik faylasuf tan olingan?", "options": ["Suqrot", "Aflotun (Platon)", "Aristotel (Arastu)", "Pifagor"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "Aristotel ''Organon'' asarida to''g''ri tafakkur mantiqiy qonuniyatlarini tizimlashtirgan."}, {"question": "''Bir vaqtda va bir nisbatda narsa ham oq, ham qora bo''la olmaydi'' qaysi mantiq qonuni?", "options": ["Ayniyat qonuni", "Ziddiyatsizlik qonuni", "Yetarli asos qonuni", "Uchinchisi istisno qonuni"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Ziddiyatsizlik qonuniga ko''ra ikkita qarama-qarshi hukm bir vaqtda haqiqat bo''la olmaydi."}, {"question": "Xususiy dalillardan umumiy xulosaga boruvchi tafakkur yo''li nima deyiladi?", "options": ["Deduksiya", "Induksiya", "Abstraksiya", "Analogiya"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Induksiya yakka holatlarni umumlashtirish orqali umumiy xulosaga olib boradi."}]'::jsonb, '["mantiq", "tafakkur", "aristotel", "sillogizm", "deduksiya", "induksiya", "universitet"]'::jsonb, 30) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
